Actually wait, let me think more carefully. "主动反馈" likely means explicit user actions (clicking helpful/unhelpful, submitting ratings). "被动反馈" likely means implicit behavioral signals the system can infer without the user explicitly providing feedback — like conversation duration, whether the user asked clarifying follow-ups, whether practice scores improved over time, RAG match quality, etc.

This is a really important distinction because:

主动反馈 (explicit): feedback_log table, practice evaluation scores (hits/misses), grain helpful/unhelpful counts
被动反馈 (implicit): conversation_stats (duration, token usage, RAG tiers), message patterns (did user rephrase twice meaning the first answer was poor?), practice improvement over time, knowledge_gap frequency, grain retrieval frequency and similarity scores
The beauty of "被动反馈" is scale — every single conversation generates passive signals without requiring any user action. These can be mined at scale to discover patterns that explicit feedback alone couldn't reveal.

